From 3bf79db50b9f470791d4fdfe309562b73598f8f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 08:44:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Shops: the touch layout, full width with a Back button

In the touch layout a shop (Shop_Run) runs across the full width: the
windows that sat at the GBA screen's right edge (coins, the bag, sell and
repair prices, quantity) keep to the right edge, and the stock row and
description lines stretch. The keeper's lines stay at the top. A Back
button sits at the top right for the whole visit: UiBackButton_Open
registers a touch zone (Touch_SetBackZone) that holds B for a frame when
tapped, so every shop screen's own key code takes it. Classic is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014ta8ykfbWFo924wEqysLhg
